<Data>Data Flow Analysis : LTE_DL_EVM Analysis2&#x000D;&#x000A;9/18/2019..2:04 PM&#x000D;&#x000A;Ambient Temperature[C]=27.0&#x000D;&#x000A;LTE_DL_MIMO_2Ant_Src_RangeCheck &apos;LTE_DL_EVM2__LTE_DL_MIMO_2Ant_Src_1.LTE_DL_MIMO_2Ant_Src_RangeCheck&apos;: &#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;System Configurations:&#x000D;&#x000A;1. Number of transmit antenna ports is 2.&#x000D;&#x000A;2. Frame structure is FDD.&#x000D;&#x000A;3. Channel bandwidth is 5 MHz.&#x000D;&#x000A;4. Cell ID is 0.&#x000D;&#x000A;5. Normal cyclic prefix is employed.&#x000D;&#x000A;6. Number of OFDM symbols used for transmission of PDCCHs of the 10 downlink subframes are {2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2}.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 1:&#x000D;&#x000A;1.HARQ closed-loop transmission is enabled.&#x000D;&#x000A;The number of HARQ processes is 8. The maximum number of HARQ transmission per each HARQ process is 4.&#x000D;&#x000A;The transport block sizes displayed following indicates the transport block size in each subframe when there is no HARQ retransmission.These values may be different in HARQ retransmission.&#x000D;&#x000A;2. The MIMO mode is spatial multiplexing (SM). Precoding with large-delay CDD is applied. According to 36.211, precoder index 0 is selected for 2 antenna ports, and precoder indices 12, 13, 14 and 15 are selected for 4 antenna ports.&#x000D;&#x000A;3. The number of code word(s) is 2; The number of layer(s) is 2&#x000D;&#x000A;4. For Codeword  1, transport block sizes of the 10 subframes are {2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555}.&#x000D;&#x000A;5. For Codeword  2, transport block sizes of the 10 subframes are {2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555, 2555}.&#x000D;&#x000A;6. For Codeword 1, modulation orders of the 10 subframes are {QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK}.&#x000D;&#x000A;7. For Codeword 2, modulation orders of the 10 subframes are {QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK, QPSK}.&#x000D;&#x000A;8. Number of allocated resource blocks (RBs) of the 10 subframes are {25, 25, 25, 25, 25, 25, 25, 25, 25, 25}.&#x000D;&#x000A;9. Number of symbols (resource elements (REs)) available for UE 1 of the 10 subframes are {2892, 3300, 3300, 3300, 3300, 3156, 3300, 3300, 3300, 3300}.&#x000D;&#x000A;10. For Codeword 1, number of channel bits for UE 1 of the 10 subframes are {5784, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6312, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6600}.&#x000D;&#x000A;11. For Codeword 2, number of channel bits for UE 1 of the 10 subframes are {5784, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6312, 6600, 6600, 6600, 6600}.&#x000D;&#x000A;12. For Codeword  1, code rates of the 10 subframes are {0.4417, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.4048, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871}.&#x000D;&#x000A;13. For Codeword  2, code rates of the 10 subframes are {0.4417, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.4048, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871, 0.3871}.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 2:No resource blocks (RBs) are allocated.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 3:No resource blocks (RBs) are allocated.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 4:No resource blocks (RBs) are allocated.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 5:No resource blocks (RBs) are allocated.&#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;For UE 6:No resource blocks (RBs) are allocated.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x2022; Information: LTE_DL_EVM &apos;LTE_DL_EVM2.L1&apos;: &#x000D;&#x000A;measurement 1 was finished and the measurement results as follows: &#x000D;&#x000A;Error Summary&#x000D;&#x000A;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#x000D;&#x000A;| EVM                                  =  -22.60dB    at Max of EVM Window Start/End&#x000D;&#x000A;| EVM Pk                             =  -13.18dB    at symbol 53, subcarrier 297&#x000D;&#x000A;| Data EVM                         =  -22.35dB&#x000D;&#x000A;| RS EVM                             =  -29.60dB&#x000D;&#x000A;| RS Tx. Power(Avg)           =  -24.98  dBm &#x000D;&#x000A;| OFDM Sym. Tx. Power     